        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Two-bedroom traditional cottage built in 1949, on a significant plot of land extending along the river, and overlooking fabulous views of Lough Swilly. An early viewing is recommended, and viewings are by appointment only.\n\nRay Cottage is a charming two-bedroom property dating from 1949, set in a beautiful and highly scenic location overlooking Lough Swilly. Situated in the picturesque Rathmullan area, the property enjoys wonderful water views and offers an appealing combination of traditional character, comfortable accommodation and an exceptional outdoor setting.\n\nThe property benefits from double or triple glazing throughout, dual heating with both an oil-fired central heating system and a solid fuel range, and generous living accommodation. The living room and one of the bedrooms enjoy particularly attractive views over Lough Swilly.\n\nOutside, the property is approached through double entrance gates, with ample parking to the side, mature trees and hedging, and a timber garden shed. A particularly notable feature is the significant plot of ground located directly across the road, extending along the river and towards Ray Bridge. Planted with numerous mature trees, this substantial riverfront garden is a rare and valuable addition to the property.\n\nDespite a tranquil setting, this property remains within easy reach of local amenities, including shops, cafés, restaurants, pubs and everyday services. Rathmullan is renowned for its beautiful sandy beaches, with a wide range of walking, sailing and watersports opportunities nearby. However, the larger towns of Ramelton, Milford and Letterkenny are also readily accessible by road, providing a comprehensive range of shopping, educational, healthcare and commercial facilities. The property is also ideally positioned for enjoying the natural beauty of the Fanad Peninsula and Wild Atlantic Way.\n\nWith its Lough Swilly outlook, substantial riverfront grounds and peaceful coastal setting, Ray Cottage presents an excellent opportunity to acquire a truly unique home.\n\n---\n\nConcrete steps lead to a partially glazed, PVC front door.\n\nEntrance Vestibule: Fully glazed, with tiled flooring, and overlooking beautiful views of Lough Swilly.\n\nA partially glazed, hardwood door leads to the living room.\n\nLiving Room: 14.4 x 14.8 ft, with vinyl flooring, and features a solid fuel range set on a tiled plinth, with a tiled surround. Dual heating is in place in this property, with the solid fuel range which heats the space, radiators, hot water, and can also be used for cooking on, in addition to Oil Fired Central Heating being in place. This space also enjoys fabulous views over the water.\n\nKitchen: 15 x 9 ft, with vinyl flooring, and extensive built-in wall and base kitchen units. Stainless steel single sink and drainer unit, with mixer tap over. \n\nSteps lead to a rear hallway, containing a utility area, with vinyl flooring. This space is plumbed for a washing machine and wired for a tumble dryer.\n\nA partially glazed, PVC door leads to the rear.\n\nMain Bathroom: Vinyl flooring, and a tiled splashback over the wash hand basin. A white three-piece suite, with a tiled bath surround, containing an electric shower over the bath. \n\nBedroom One: 14.7 x 11.9 ft, double aspect, with carpet flooring. \n\nBedroom Two: 14.5 x 11.7 ft, with vinyl flooring and overlooking beautiful Lough Swilly views. \n\nOutside: The property is accessed via double entrance gates, with ample parking on the gravelled area to the side. A concrete path surrounds the house, with mature trees and hedging to boundaries. A timber garden shed is also present to the rear. Across the road from the property, there is a garden, planted with numerous trees, which runs directly to the river, and up towards Ray bridge.\n\nDisclaimer - The above particulars are issued by Glen Estates on the understanding that all negotiations are conducted through them. Information contained in the brochure does not form any part of any offer or contract and is provided in good faith, for guidance only. Glen estates have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. Maps and plans are not to scale and measurements are approximate, photographs provided for guidance only. The particulars, descriptions, dimensions, references to condition, permissions or licences for use or occupation, access and any other details, such as prices, rents or any other outgoings are for guidance only and may be subject to change. Intending purchasers / tenants must satisfy themselves as to the accuracy of details provided to them either verbally or as part of this brochure. Neither Glen Estates or any of its employees have any authority to make or give any representation or warranty in respect of this property.\n"
      },
